## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of end-to-end event-driven AWS patterns, from S3 events to Lambda processing to DynamoDB storage, with proper IAM scoping and TLS enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- S3 Event Notifications
- Lambda execution roles (least privilege)
- DynamoDB PutItem permissions
- S3 bucket policy TLS enforcement
- Security without public access and basic end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::company-logs/app1/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["dynamodb:PutItem"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:REGION:ACCOUNT_ID:table/App1LogSummary"
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::company-logs/app1/*",
      "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "false"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

